WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:02.310
"A sixth film in this franchise..."

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.549
“They are finally working on a new Final
Destination movie.”

00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:09.240
“They basically announced that this is in
the works over at New Line,

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.009
another Final Destination movie.”

00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:13.190
Final Destination 6.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.190
It’s happening.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:18.330
But after covering near death experiences
involving a plane crash, highway pile-up,

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.701
rollercoaster derail, NASCAR d-sas-tar, and a
bridge collapse, what is in store for the

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:24.940
next installment of Final Destination?

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.760
Could fan-favorite character William Bludworth
be involved?

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.456
Stay tuned.

00:00:32.853 --> 00:00:36.800
"We're toying with having it take place in
the world of first responders: EMTs, firemen

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.190
and police,” Perry said.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:41.400
“These people deal with death on the front
lines every day, and make choices that can

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.890
cause people to live or die…

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:46.601
We're thinking that world might be an interesting
way into a Final Destination movie, and one

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:49.890
which can also generate unique set pieces
in a very credible way."

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:53.770
That’s what series producer Craig Perry
had to say about the next Final Destination,

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:56.710
but what I want to know is how this actually
fits into the canon.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:00.750
As someone who made a 30 minute video where
I basically put everything, the movies, books

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:04.260
and comics into chronological order, I want
to know where this movie takes place.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.929
The lore is important to me.

00:01:05.929 --> 00:01:10.240
The danger with coming out with a new installment
after a long gap, is that these tend to reboot

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:13.240
the franchise, which means we’d be starting
over with all new lore.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:17.139
However, according to an interview series
creator Jeffrey Reddick had with BD, that

00:01:17.139 --> 00:01:20.680
will probably not be the case with the new
Final Destination, but it will be set in a

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.869
“different world”.

00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:22.920
So what does that mean?

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.770
A couple of possibilities come to mind.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:28.539
There’s one scene that has always intrigued
me most about the original Final Destination,

00:01:28.539 --> 00:01:31.479
and it’s not that part where Death hides
the evidence of how it took out Tod even though

00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:33.649
nothing else like that happens in any of the
other movies.

00:01:33.649 --> 00:01:37.020
It’s the part where Clear and Alex sit on
the beach together, look up at the stars,

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.680
and wonder what life would be like if the
disasters that impacted both of their lives

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.083
had never happened.

00:01:43.954 --> 00:01:49.106
ALEX: "You thing they're still up there? Somehow. Flight 180, are they still in flight?

00:01:49.219 --> 00:01:52.253
Somewhere, are they safe?"

00:01:52.254 --> 00:01:57.986
CLEAR: "I have thought a lot about that somewhere Alex. It exists, that place. 

00:01:57.986 --> 00:02:01.995
Where my Dad is still safe and I have no idea about this life here.

00:02:04.393 --> 00:02:07.316
Where our friends are still in the sky.

00:02:08.273 --> 00:02:11.470
Where everyone gets a second chance."

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:12.760
It exists.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.849
A world where Flight 180 landed safely, exists.

00:02:15.849 --> 00:02:18.640
What if Final Destination has a split timeline?

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:20.689
I would argue that it already does.

00:02:20.689 --> 00:02:24.200
In the original movie, Flight 180 went down
in the year 1999.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.030
But in each of the sequels, the event took
place in 2000.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:31.530
Sure, this might just be a retcon, but I’ve
come to justify it as two similar timelines,

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:34.940
where most of the events are the same, but
in the sequel universe, everything takes place

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:35.940
a year later.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.410
In fact, the very concept of the series seems
to prove this to be true.

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:42.989
The visions that each protagonist has are
what is supposed to happen, but they make

00:02:42.989 --> 00:02:45.510
changes; they alter their destinies to survive.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:48.319
Each time this happens, they create a new
split in the timeline.

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:52.269
The world where they don’t intervene…
it exists, they just didn’t go down that

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:53.269
path.

00:02:53.269 --> 00:02:54.769
The original five are a set.

00:02:54.769 --> 00:02:55.769
They go together.

00:02:55.769 --> 00:02:58.680
I think there’s no way to avoid the next
movie feeling different given how much time

00:02:58.680 --> 00:02:59.680
has passed.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.870
It’s like how you can put an “old photo
filter” on a new photo, but it never feels

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.840
quite the same as a picture that was taken
during that era.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.829
So making a new continuity on a new timeline
branch would help alleviate that issue and

00:03:09.829 --> 00:03:13.459
prevent the new movie from stepping on the
original five, which could upset fans.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:17.760
We’ve seen this approach taken with the
Halloween franchise basically becoming a choose-your-own-adventure,

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.099
but the idea fits much better with Final Destination
where there’s an in-universe explanation

00:03:22.099 --> 00:03:23.099
for it.

00:03:23.099 --> 00:03:26.209
But what if I’m taking Jeffrey Reddick’s
word a little too literally?

00:03:26.209 --> 00:03:29.690
Maybe when he said it takes place in “a
new world” all he meant was that instead

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:32.590
of taking place in the world of teenagers
and young adults, it takes place

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:35.290
in the world of emergency responders and health
care workers.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.937
Speaking of which, there’s something I have
to do.

00:03:39.532 --> 00:03:43.785
🎵 Epic Triumph Music 🎵

00:04:14.719 --> 00:04:19.220
If we EVER want to see Final Destination 6,
it’s entirely dependent on ending the COVID-19

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.170
pandemic, and it’s becoming clear that the
only way that’s gonna happen, is if the

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.700
population gets vaccinated.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:27.100
I wanted to show my experience so that everyone
knows there’s nothing to be afraid of.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.080
The needle is so small, you don’t even feel
it go in.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.310
I had a little bit of soreness for the next
day or two, but it was never painful.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:35.790
The night after the second dose I was feverish
and had chills and a headache, but there was

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:39.030
never a moment where I felt scared, because
I knew that this was the vaccine going to

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:42.290
work in my body to protect me, and the vaccine
doesn’t contain the virus.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:45.880
How it works is the vaccine basically contains
the instructions that teach your body how

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:49.090
to produce the viral proteins that will be
recognized by your immune system.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:53.110
So if the virus, Sars-Cov-2 enters your system,
your body will already know how to defeat

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:54.730
it, and prevent you from getting COVID-19.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:58.760
It’s basically your Final Destination vision
that can protect you from disaster, because

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:02.790
without the vaccine, you could become infected,
and nobody can predict how sick you might

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:07.260
get -- it could be mild, severe or life threatening,
not to mention other symptoms that may last

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.480
for months or longer.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:12.420
Don’t worry, I made sure to run that by
a few medical professionals before I said

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:13.750
it out loud on the internet.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:17.170
I certainly hope the new Final Destination
isn’t about a pandemic though.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:19.980
I think this era represents a cultural shift
for us.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:25.140
Horror was super popular from 2014-2018 with
a lot of darker stories like IT, Split and

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:29.110
A Quiet Place, and I can see the genre swinging
back to something more lighthearted, much

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:33.100
how like Grunge was the dark and serious dominant
genre of the 90s, but it got a little too

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.790
depressing for people after Kurt Cobain, and
that’s when we started seeing the snot-nosed

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:41.520
pop punk acts blowing up: Blink-182, Sum 41,
Green Day 75.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.570
So I think the time is going to be right for
a Final Destination 6.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:47.860
They’ve got the perfect writers for it,
Marcus Dunstan and Patrick Melton, the guys

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.310
who did Saw 4-7.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:52.630
What makes Saw such an awesome franchise is
that the later sequels don’t suck that much

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:55.130
for the most part and they even honor the
continuity.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:59.030
It feels right for these guys to give that
same treatment to the other big 2000s horror

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.030
series.

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:03.420
Jeffrey Reddick has insisted that the sixth
is not a reboot, but curiously mentions another

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.420
world.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:05.880
The statement seems to contradict itself.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.490
I’ve explored that the movie might look
like if we take his words literally, but about

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:10.910
if the we them figuratively.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:15.550
Operating in the world of first responders,
EMT, firemen and police affords an interesting

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:19.340
opportunity, these are all government workers
that might show up the scene of a disaster

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:22.570
and are likely to have interactions with a
medical examiner.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:24.460
Could we see the return of William Bludworth?

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:27.790
When I made the Horror History episode on
Bludworth, I theorized that he could have

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:29.710
been an escapee of Death’s design.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:33.070
This character is shrouded in mystery, and
I always thought it would be cool to explore

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:36.560
his past and learn how he came to be so knowledgeable
about how death operates.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:40.070
I think it would definitely be interesting
to see a prequel, where a young Bludworth

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:43.890
sees the horrors of how his choices affect
people’s lives on the front line, and transitions

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:47.550
to the role of medical examiner so that he
can become an expert on death, namely how

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.550
to avoid it.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:52.160
If you want to hear more about my theory,
click that video on the left and if you love

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.990
horror, remember to subscribe to CZsWorld
for new horrors every week, ring the deathbell

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:59.580
and select all notifications and I’ll see
you in the next one.

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:01.590
Assuming we both survive.

